# Rules the 2018 engine did not have: Destructive Dilemma (DD), Absorption
# (ABS) and Quantifier Negation (QN). The format is described in ../README.md.

# --- Destructive Dilemma: (p → q) & (r → s), ~q | ~s ∴ ~p | ~r ---

case: dd-basic
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(P → Q) & (R → S)//~Q | ~S=>~P | ~R}
3. ~P | ~R ; 1,2 DD
expect: valid

case: dd-citations-reversed
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(P → Q) & (R → S)//~Q | ~S=>~P | ~R}
3. ~P | ~R ; 2,1 DD
expect: valid

case: dd-in-a-proof
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(A → B) & (C → D)//~B=>~A | ~C}
3. ~B | ~D ; 2 ADD
4. ~A | ~C ; 1,3 DD
expect: valid

case: dd-denying-the-antecedents
source: soundness, rule added in 2026
problem: {(P → Q) & (R → S)//~P | ~R=>~Q | ~S}
3. ~Q | ~S ; 1,2 DD
expect: invalid at 3: DD needs ~Q | ~S and gives ~P | ~R
argument: invalid

# --- Absorption: p → q ∴ p → (p & q) ---

case: abs-basic
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {P → Q=>P → (P & Q)}
2. P → (P & Q) ; 1 ABS
expect: valid

case: abs-commuted-conjunction
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {P → Q=>P → (Q & P)}
2. P → (Q & P) ; 1 ABS
strict: invalid at 2: ABS gives P → (P & Q)
flexible: valid

case: abs-wrong-antecedent
source: soundness, rule added in 2026
problem: {P → Q=>Q → (P & Q)}
2. Q → (P & Q) ; 1 ABS
expect: invalid at 2: ABS gives P → (P & Q)
argument: invalid

# --- Quantifier Negation: ~(∀x)Φ ≡ (∃x)~Φ, ~(∃x)Φ ≡ (∀x)~Φ, (∀x)Φ ≡ ~(∃x)~Φ, (∃x)Φ ≡ ~(∀x)~Φ ---

case: qn-not-every
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {~(∀x)Fx=>(∃x)~Fx}
2. (∃x)~Fx ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-some-not
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(∃x)~Fx=>~(∀x)Fx}
2. ~(∀x)Fx ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-not-some
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {~(∃x)Fx=>(∀x)~Fx}
2. (∀x)~Fx ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-every-not
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(∀x)~Fx=>~(∃x)Fx}
2. ~(∃x)Fx ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-every-as-not-some-not
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(∀x)Fx=>~(∃x)~Fx}
2. ~(∃x)~Fx ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-some-as-not-every-not
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {(∃x)Fx=>~(∀x)~Fx}
2. ~(∀x)~Fx ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-inside-a-line
source: rule added in 2026
problem: {P → ~(∀x)(Fx → Gx)=>P → (∃x)~(Fx → Gx)}
2. P → (∃x)~(Fx → Gx) ; 1 QN
expect: valid

case: qn-in-a-proof
source: rule added in 2026, in the style of Copi's exercises
problem: {~(∃x)(Fx & ~Gx)=>(∀x)(Fx → Gx)}
2. (∀x)~(Fx & ~Gx) ; 1 QN
3. ~(Fy & ~Gy) ; 2 UI
4. ~Fy | ~~Gy ; 3 DM
5. ~Fy | Gy ; 4 DN
6. Fy → Gy ; 5 IMPL
7. (∀x)(Fx → Gx) ; 6 UG
expect: valid

case: qn-with-ei
source: rule added in 2026, in the style of Copi's exercises
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → Gx)//~(∀x)Gx=>(∃x)~Fx}
3. (∃x)~Gx ; 2 QN
4. ~Ga ; 3 EI
5. Fa → Ga ; 1 UI
6. ~Fa ; 5,4 MT
7. (∃x)~Fx ; 6 EG
expect: valid

case: qn-keeps-the-quantifier
source: soundness, rule added in 2026
problem: {~(∀x)Fx=>(∀x)~Fx}
2. (∀x)~Fx ; 1 QN
expect: invalid at 2: QN turns ~(∀x)Fx into (∃x)~Fx; not every F does not mean every thing is not F
argument: invalid

case: qn-loses-a-negation
source: soundness, rule added in 2026
problem: {~(∃x)Fx=>(∃x)~Fx}
2. (∃x)~Fx ; 1 QN
expect: invalid at 2: QN turns ~(∃x)Fx into (∀x)~Fx
